# Third-party notices\par
\par
Syndocal dynamically links FFmpeg shared libraries for video decoding, including\par
H.264, H.265, HAP, DXV, ProRes, VP9 and AV1. The normal Windows variant uses\par
FFmpeg `n8.1.3-9-g29e619e767`, self-built by Syndocal's GitHub Actions workflow\par
from the BtbN FFmpeg-Builds recipe with the Chromaprint and FFTW3 recipes\par
removed (inventory version `n8.1.3-9-g29e619e767-20260930-syndocal-r40366564270`;\par
the DLLs self-report `n8.1.3-9-g29e619e767-20260930`), reporting LGPL version 3\par
or later. Its measured configure line enables shared libraries and version 3\par
licensing, and contains neither `--enable-gpl`, `--enable-nonfree` nor\par
`--enable-chromaprint`; none of the seven DLLs contains a Chromaprint or FFTW\par
string. The upstream LGPL self-description is not a completed license audit.\par
Publication is blocked until the actual build inputs/linkage and resulting\par
license obligations are reconciled;\par
the collected notices do not grant release clearance or establish exact binary\par
dependency closure.\par
