## Open Fixture Library (bundled fixture profiles)\par
\par
Syndocal bundles a converted snapshot of the Open Fixture Library so that\par
manufacturer fixture profiles are available offline, with no account or\par
download, on first launch.\par
\par
- Source: https://github.com/OpenLightingProject/open-fixture-library\par
- Snapshot revision: `c08598f45ce5e7cff4089a65bb67b5ba2777ee32` (recorded in the\par
  bundle's `sourceRevision` field; regenerate with\par
  `node scripts/build-ofl-library.mjs <checkout> <sha>`)\par
- License: MIT\par
- Copyright (c) 2017 Florian & Felix Edelmann and OFL contributors\par
- License text: `licenses/open-fixture-library-MIT.txt`\par
\par
The bundled data is a lossy conversion: each mode is reduced to its ordered\par
DMX attribute layout (the same representation Syndocal uses for its own custom\par
profiles). Matrix channel insert blocks are expanded before conversion.\par
Capability ranges, wheel slot media, and physical data are not carried over -\par
operators who need the full definition download the manufacturer's GDTF from\par
GDTF Share.\par
\par
## Q Light Controller Plus fixture definitions (bundled fixture profiles)\par
\par
Syndocal also bundles a converted snapshot of QLC+'s fixture definitions as a\par
supplemental offline source. Open Fixture Library has higher precedence: exact\par
normalized manufacturer/model conflicts are omitted from the QLC+ bundle and\par
recorded in its conversion audit.\par
\par
- Source: https://github.com/mcallegari/qlcplus\par
- Snapshot revision: `18cf9da9934e5ea0b5026dd43b0f48be1e5b9550` (recorded in the\par
  bundle's `sourceRevision` field; regenerate after the OFL bundle with\par
  `node scripts/build-qlc-library.mjs <checkout> <sha>`)\par
- License: Apache-2.0\par
- Copyright QLC+ contributors and fixture definition authors\par
- License text: `licenses/qlcplus-Apache-2.0.txt`\par
\par
This is the same lossy ordered-DMX-layout conversion described above. Adjacent\par
coarse/fine pairs are represented as 16-bit controls; unrecognized channel\par
semantics remain addressable as numbered generic controls so the source mode's\par
DMX footprint is preserved exactly.\par
